WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.840
- Give it up for my band, y'all.

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.673
As I was saying, everybody.

00:00:02.673 --> 00:00:04.885
(cheering)

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.150
I love...
Don't kill...

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.170
everybody.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.940
That song was "Walkaway Joe,"

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.520
by Ms. Trisha Yearwood and Don Henley.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.830
I love Trisha Yearwood, y'all.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.160
Seriously, one of my favorite
singers on the planet.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.300
Let's meet Matthew who
requested that song.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.750
So where are you at, Matthew?

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:21.610
- It's Matthew McConaughey!
- Austin, Texas.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.887
Hi there, Kelly.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.390
- How are you doing?

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.790
- Relatively pretty well.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.980
We're trying to get over
this freeze down here.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.170
You know, it kinda knocked
some of us back a hair.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.230
But well, overall we're doing pretty good.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.063
- Yeah. Oh my God.

00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:38.610
That's good to hear. That's good to hear.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.620
Why did you request "Walkaway Joe?"

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.540
- Well, "Walkaway Joe."

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.160
And it was, think it was early 1992.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.460
I'm going to college here
at the University of Texas.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.550
This is before "Days and Confused."

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.610
And I was trying to get odd jobs

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:53.760
in front of the camera when I could.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.760
And I got cast in that
music video to play Joe.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.800
Things are going well then
where we end up the last stop

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.790
she wakes up and "Joe,"
myself, is nowhere to be seen.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.568
Therefore, AKA the title, "Walkaway Joe."

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:11.298
- [Kelly] I love that
though. Do you remember?

00:01:11.298 --> 00:01:12.897
I love that about country music videos,

00:01:12.897 --> 00:01:15.740
especially in like the 90s,
there would be such a story,

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:16.573
like a plot.

00:01:16.573 --> 00:01:18.450
Like, they'd have actors, real big actors.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.710
And I think that's amazing.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:20.810
I didn't know that was your first thing.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.540
I didn't know that was
before "Dazed and Confused."

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.050
It's amazing.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:25.190
- That, and "Unsolved Mysteries."

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.210
Yeah, "Walkaway Joe" was my first time

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.166
in front of the camera.
(laughing)

00:01:29.166 --> 00:01:32.416
And I still don't believe
I've met Trisha in person.

00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:35.930
- Did you just say that
and "Unsolved Mysteries?"

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.004
- [Matthew] Yes.
- I love you so much!

00:01:37.004 --> 00:01:38.414
(laughing)

00:01:38.414 --> 00:01:39.247
That's amazing.

